A program executes three fork() calls one after another, with no conditions and no exits:
```c
fork();
fork();
fork();
```
How many processes exist at the end, counting the original?

How many child processes does the following create (the original process is not a child)?
```c
for (i = 0; i < 4; i++)
    fork();
```

What does the parent print?
```c
int x = 10;
if (fork() == 0) {
    x = x + 5;
} else {
    wait(NULL);
    printf("%d", x);
}
```

How many child processes does this program create?
```c
for (i = 0; i < 12; i++)
    if (i % 3 == 0)
        fork();
```

How many processes (counting the original) exist after both statements finish?
```c
fork() && fork();
fork() || fork();
```

How many times is printf executed?
```c
for (i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    if (fork() == 0)
        break;
}
printf("x");
```

Standard output is unbuffered, so every printf appears at once. How many characters are printed in total?
```c
printf("A");
fork();
printf("B");
fork();
printf("C");
```

How many times is printf executed in total?
```c
int x = 2;
while (x > 0) {
    fork();
    printf("hi");
    wait(NULL);
    x--;
}
```

How many child processes are created?
```c
for (i = 0; i < 3; i++)
    for (j = 0; j < 2; j++)
        fork();
```

How many processes exist after the loop ends (counting the original)?
```c
for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
    if (fork() == 0) {
        fork();
    }
}
```

Each process prints its own value of n at the end. What is the sum of all printed values?
```c
int n = 0;
if (fork()) n += 1;
if (fork()) n += 2;
if (fork()) n += 4;
printf("%d ", n);
```

How many times is printf executed?
```c
for (i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    if (fork() == 0)
        continue;
    break;
}
fork();
printf("x");
```

Assume every fork succeeds and stdout is unbuffered. How many characters are printed in total?
```c
if (fork() == 0) {
    fork();
    printf("C");
    exit(0);
}
wait(NULL);
printf("P");
```

Consider the program below. Each character is printed atomically and appears as soon as it is printed.
```c
if (fork() == 0) {
    printf("A");
} else {
    printf("B");
    wait(NULL);
    printf("C");
}
printf("D");
```
